  "description_md": "Given a string, decide whether it reads the same forwards and backwards once you strip out everything except letters and digits and lowercase everything.\n\n**Example:** `\"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\"` becomes `\"amanaplanacanalpanama\"` after cleaning, which is a palindrome, so the answer is `true`. `\"race a car\"` becomes `\"raceacar\"`, which is not a palindrome, so the answer is `false`.\n\n**Constraints:** string length up to ~10^5; may contain letters, digits, spaces, and punctuation.",
