  "description_md": "Design a stack that supports the usual `push`/`pop`/`top` operations plus retrieving the minimum element currently on the stack, all in O(1) time.\n\n**Example:** push `-2`, `0`, `-3`; `getMin()` returns `-3`; `pop()` removes `-3`; `top()` returns `0`; `getMin()` now returns `-2`.\n\n**Constraints:** `pop`, `top`, and `getMin` are only ever called on a non-empty stack; values fit in a 32-bit signed integer.",
